      "writtenOn": "2023-10-30T10:47:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why can each IpServer tell BpfCoordinator to stop and start individual parts of BPF offload? Could we simplify it so that an IpServer just tells BpfCoordinator when it needs BPF or not? IpServer could do something like:\n\n    mBpfCoordinator.addIpServer(this, mInterfaceParams);\n\nonce it\u0027s ready to start and its interface params are known. Then, when it stops (perhaps in TetheredState#exit), it could do something like:\n\n    mBpfCoordinator.removeIpServer(this);\n\nLooking at the comments in startServingInterface, it looks like we\u0027re not sure if it\u0027s possible to ensure the interface params are correct for bluetooth; I think that\u0027s probably because the interface params might end up being null sometimes. But maybe we can just put the call to mBpfCoordinator.addIpServer at the end of BaseServingState#enter, inside an if (mInterfaceParams !\u003d  null).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 636,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 636,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "12cd020d549089215a85e0dc8eeeb295e5b1054c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
