      "writtenOn": "2023-10-30T10:47:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of starting and stopping mIpNeighborMonitor based on what IpServers do, why not start / stop IpNeighborMonitor in BpfCoordinator#startPolling  / BpfCoordinator#stopPolling?\n\nAt the moment there doesn\u0027t seem to be a need to start monitoring for neighbours on individual interfaces, because IpServer it starts monitoring when it\u0027s constructed.\n\nThere might be a need to stop monitoring when an IpServer is totally finished (UnavailableState#enter) perhaps?\n\nBut see other comments about having a single register/unregister method for IpServer.",
